      "end_reason": "eos_token",
      "raw_text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine the total number of eggs required and then divide that by the number of eggs received per babysitting session.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total number of eggs needed.**\nSandra needs to make 15 Spanish flans.\nEach flan requires 3 eggs.\nTotal eggs needed = $15 \\text{ flans} \\times 3 \\text{ eggs/flan} = 45 \\text{ eggs}$.\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the number of babysitting sessions required.**\nSandra receives a basket of 9 eggs every time she babysits.\nTo find out how many times she needs to babysit to get 45 eggs, we divide the total eggs needed by the eggs received per session.\nNumber of sessions = $\\frac{\\text{Total eggs needed}}{\\text{Eggs per session}}$\nNumber of sessions = $\\frac{45}{9} = 5$.\n\nSo, Sandra needs to babysit 5 times.\n\n#### 5<|im_end|>",
      "answer_text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine the total number of eggs required and then divide that by the number of eggs received per babysitting session.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total number of eggs needed.**\nSandra needs to make 15 Spanish flans.\nEach flan requires 3 eggs.\nTotal eggs needed = $15 \\text{ flans} \\times 3 \\text{ eggs/flan} = 45 \\text{ eggs}$.\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the number of babysitting sessions required.**\nSandra receives a basket of 9 eggs every time she babysits.\nTo find out how many times she needs to babysit to get 45 eggs, we divide the total eggs needed by the eggs received per session.\nNumber of sessions = $\\frac{\\text{Total eggs needed}}{\\text{Eggs per session}}$\nNumber of sessions = $\\frac{45}{9} = 5$.\n\nSo, Sandra needs to babysit 5 times.\n\n#### 5",
      "input_sha256": "7208fe230ac9ac61e380ed42194df7ff64bde9a8504ad9ccaf3d5305b3eebb46",
      "parsed_answer": "5",
      "correct": true
    }
